  {
    "title": "ا after fatha is a long “aa”",
    "body": "Alif after a fatha stretches the “a” to twice its length, as in “baa”. Written “aa” in the respellings. At the start of a word alif is a hamza seat or a helper vowel instead (see those rules).",
    "pattern": "\\u064E\\u0651?\\u0627(?!\\p{L}(?:\\u0652|(?!\\p{M})))",
    "examples": [
      {
        "word": "كَانَ",
        "say": "KAA-na",
