  {
    "title": "Hamzat al-wasl: a bare ا at the start of a word is skipped",
    "body": "A plain ا with no mark at the start of a word (in ال, اسْم, ابْن…) is a helper vowel. Said first, it is “a” in ال and “i” elsewhere (sometimes “u”). After another word it is silent and the words join.",
    "pattern": "(?<![\\p{L}\\p{M}])(?:[\\u0648\\u0641\\u0628\\u0643]\\p{M}+)?\\u0627(?=\\p{L}(?:\\u0652|(?!\\p{M})))",
    "examples": [
      {
        "word": "اسْمِي",
        "say": "IS-mee",
        "en": "my name"
      },
      {
        "word": "ابْنِي",
        "say": "IB-nee",
        "en": "my son"
      },
      {
        "word": "وَالشَّايَ",
        "say": "wash-SHAA-ya",
        "en": "and the tea"
      },
      {
        "word": "وَالْقَهْوَةَ",
        "say": "wal-QAH-wa-ta",
        "en": "and the coffee"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "At a pause, drop the last short vowel",
    "body": "Before a full stop or comma, drop the final short vowel or “-un”, “-in”; ـًا becomes “-aa”, ة is just “a”. A long syllable left at the end takes the stress: كَبِيرٌ becomes “ka-BEER”.",
    "pattern": "[\\u064B-\\u0650]\\u0651?\\u0627?(?=\\s*[.،!؟:؛…»]|\\n|$)",
    "examples": [
      {
        "word": "الْبَيْتِ",
        "say": "al-BAYT",
        "en": "the house (at a pause)"
      },
      {
        "word": "كَبِيرٌ",
        "say": "ka-BEER",
        "en": "big (at a pause)"
      },
      {
        "word": "سَاعَةٍ",
        "say": "SAA-ʿa",
        "en": "an hour (at a pause)"
      },
      {
        "word": "جِدًّا",
        "say": "JID-daa",
        "en": "very (at a pause)"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Hamza (ء أ إ ؤ ئ) is a catch in the throat",
    "body": "Hamza is a short stop of the breath, like the break in “uh-oh”. It sits alone (ء) or on a seat, ا, و or ى-shape (أ إ ؤ ئ); the seat is silent. Written ' in the respellings, left out at the start of a word.",
    "pattern": "[\\u0621\\u0623\\u0625\\u0624\\u0626]",
    "examples": [
      {
        "word": "وَأَنَا",
        "say": "wa-'A-naa",
        "en": "and I"
