  {
    "title": "ة (ta marbuta) is “t” before an ending, “a” at a pause",
    "body": "ة, an ه with two dots, ends many feminine words. Before the vowel ending it is a “t”: ـَةً “-tan”, ـَةِ “-ti”. At the end of a sentence the ending drops and only “a” is heard.",
    "pattern": "\\u0629",
